{
  "name": "FEBIAC Taxo comparison set, three regions, October 2026",
  "capturedBy": "Pax, Proxem AI",
  "capturedOn": "2026-10-01 to 2026-10-06",
  "source": "FEBIAC Taxo Lite, https://dataservices.febiac.be/en/taxo/online",
  "tariffVersionAtCapture": "2026.09.2",
  "method": "The Taxo wizard was driven through its own web form, one submission at a time, five a day against its undisclosed free-tier limit of five calculations. One submission returns all three regions at once: there is no region selector, so every submission below yields three directly comparable figures off the same result screen. The per-region response data was read separately to confirm that identical Brussels and Wallonia road tax figures are real and not one results cell read twice. Raw captures: febiac-taxo-results.json (batch 1) and febiac-taxo-day1/2/3.json.",
  "fixedInputs": "Price 35000 EUR excluding VAT and discount 0 throughout: both are required fields in the wizard and neither feeds BIV or road tax in Belgian law. Taxo has no CO2 cycle selector and no particulate filter input, so the Euro 4 soot filter branch (task 117) cannot be tested against it at all. Fiscal HP is a separate field from cylinder capacity and the wizard derives neither from the other, so every case below records fiscalHp explicitly, even where it equals the cc-derived value.",
  "tolerance": 0.05,
  "notes": [
    "The official block is measured ground truth. Do not edit it.",
    "engineAtCapture is a snapshot of core/tax.js at tariff version 2026.09.2 BEFORE the four approved fixes, kept as the baseline the fixes are measured against. It is not a target.",
    "status expect: the comparison gates the build under --strict. status known-mismatch: reported on every run, never gating, each one carrying the reason and the task it belongs to. Freezing a known defect as expected would hide it; excluding it would lose it.",
    "W-OLDTIMER (submission 12: petrol, 250 g, Euro 0, 110 kW, registered 1994-01-01) returned HTTP 500 from FEBIAC and is absent from this file. A 500 is an unhandled server error rather than an out-of-domain rejection, and submissions 6 and 11 show that age alone up to 18 years is accepted, so the likely trigger is the Euro 0 category. There is nothing to freeze for it.",
    "Wallonia BIV, Brussels road tax and Wallonia road tax expectations are FEBIAC's own reported figures, which the four approved fixes bring the engine to. The pre-fix engine value is in engineAtCapture: that is the thing this fixture exists to catch, not the thing it should expect."
  ],
